{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.sub_top_inversion_after","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.sub_top_inversion_after","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradePromotion.lean#L77-L88","doc":"After swapping the top two points, the pair `(sub, top)` **is** an inversion:\nthe fresh generator turns the one non-inversion it can see into an inversion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.sub_top_not_inversion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.sub_top_not_inversion","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradePromotion.lean#L69-L75","doc":"In particular the second-from-top point lands strictly below the top, so the\npair `(sub, top)` is **not** an inversion of `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.lt_top_of_fixes_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.lt_top_of_fixes_top","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradePromotion.lean#L58-L67","doc":"**The key step.** A permutation fixing the top point must send every other\npoint strictly below the top -- by injectivity, since the top is already taken,\nand it is the maximum. This is what makes the fresh generator length-increasing\nrather than length-decreasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.sub_lt_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.sub_lt_top","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradePromotion.lean#L55-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.sub","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradePromotion.lean#L52-L53","doc":"The point just below the top. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.top","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradePromotion.lean#L49-L50","doc":"The top point of `Fin (n+2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.length","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradePromotion.lean#L46-L47","doc":"Coxeter length = inversion count = GS filtration grade. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.invSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.JetGradePromotion.invSet","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/JetGradePromotion.lean#L40-L44","doc":"The inversion set of a permutation of `Fin m`: ordered pairs it reverses.\nThis is the Coxeter length's combinatorial model, and the GS filtration grade\nof the basis element `T_w`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}